zlib_deflate

 SYNOPSIS
  Compress a string

 USAGE
  zstr = zlib_deflate (str)

 DESCRIPTION

 QUALIFIERS
  ; level=val:
  ; method=val:
  ; wbits=val:
  ; memlevel=val:
  ; strategy=val:

 EXAMPLE

 NOTES

 SEE ALSO
  zlib_inflate, zlib_inflate_new

--------------------------------------------------------------

zlib_deflate_new

 SYNOPSIS
  Create a zlib deflation object

 USAGE
  zlibobj = zlib_deflate_new ()

 DESCRIPTION

 QUALIFIERS
  ; level=val: one of: ZLIB_NO_COMPRESSION, ZLIB_BEST_SPEED,
ZLIB_BEST_COMPRESSION,
ZLIB_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION (default: ZLIB_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION)
  ; method=val: ZLIB_DEFLATED (default: ZLIB_DEFLATED)
  ; wbits=val: Window size in bits, 8-15 is recommended (default: 15)
  ; memlevel=val: Specifies the amount of memory to use; 1-9,
default=8
  ; strategy=val: one of: ZLIB_DEFAULT_STRATEGY, ZLIB_FILTERED,
ZLIB_HUFFMAN_ONLY, ZLIB_RLE,ZLIB_FIXED (default: ZLIB_DEFAULT_STRATEGY)

 METHODS
  ..deflate : compress a string
  ..reset : Resets the stream keeping various state parameters
  ..flush : Flush pending output to the output buffer

 EXAMPLE

 NOTES
 See the zlib compression library documentation for more information
 regarding the qualifiers and methods.  Note that this module uses ZLIB as a
 prefix whereas the underlying library API uses Z, e.g.,
 `ZLIB_FIXED' vs `Z_FIXED'.

 SEE ALSO
  zlib_deflate, zlib_inflate_new

--------------------------------------------------------------

